 "result_text": "`git machete github checkout-pr` now says when a PR is closed instead of reporting it as not found. I haven't run it or any tests, so the change is untested.\n\nIf the PR isn't among the open ones, it makes one more API call (`GET /repos/{org}/{repo}/pulls/{number}`) to look up its state. A closed PR gets this message:\n\n```\nPR #204 is already closed in repository `org/repo`\n```\n\nIf the lookup fails, for example with a 404 because the PR never existed, you still get the original \"is not found\" message. A merged PR is also closed on GitHub, so it gets the \"already closed\" message too.\n\nThe new lookup function is `derive_pull_request_state` in `git_machete/github.py`. The check itself is in `checkout_github_prs` in `git_machete/client.py`.",
